<title>USA: Seven Seas mutual funds change name to SSgA.</title>
<headline>Seven Seas mutual funds change name to SSgA.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seven Seas Investment Portfolios said Wednesday it will change its name of its family of 14 mutual funds to SSgA Funds to conform to the name of its parent State Street Global Advisors, a State Street Boston Corp affiliate.</p>
<p>SSgA's nine stock and bond funds will also be available through Charles Schwab Corp's Institutional Marketplace, State Street said. The 14 mutual funds, targeted towards institutional clients but also available to retail customers, manage more than $8.5 billion in assets.</p>
<p>-- Boston bureau (617) 367-4176</p>
</text>
